    "passage": "Tom had brought a new card game to school. At lunch, he put the cards on a table and waited. Mia stopped to look, but she did not sit down. Tom began explaining every rule, speaking faster each time she looked towards the door. Then Mia pointed at the clock and said she had only five minutes before music. Tom looked at the large pile of cards in front of him. He put most of them back in the box and left six on the table. They played one short round before Mia had to go. At the door, she asked him to bring the whole game tomorrow. Tom packed the cards with a smile. This time, he put two chairs beside the table before leaving.",
